event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0c1bbaee4dd80661016aa3e80c461487d2ae45d60cc594c4d6","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":5373,"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for CBTRN02C posting, CBACT04C interest generation, and CBTRN03C\n    reporting. Each POST represents one program invocation, not an entire job\n    schedule. JSON arrays carry sequential input and output records in order;\n    indexed files remain deployment-bound persistent dependencies. HTTP paths,\n    JSON names, and status codes are chosen transport conventions, not COBOL\n    interfaces. A completed posting run may contain business rejects and still\n    returns HTTP 200. HTTP 500 represents an observed fatal execution path,\n    not a business validation rejection.\n\n    Fixed-width alphanumeric fields accept arbitrary text up to their picture\n    length, including blanks and unknown codes. Transport mapping right-pads\n    shorter text with spaces; it does not parse dates or validate card numbers.\n    Numeric JSON values represent valid numeric picture contents. No promise is\n    made about malformed native numeric encodings, arithmetic overflow, or\n    runtime availability. Output text may retain trailing spaces.\n\n    No operation implies transaction atomicity, rollback, retries, or execution\n    of SORT, IDCAMS, REPROC, backup, reload, or any subsequent batch program.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - CEE3ABD is called with code 999 and timing 0 but its implementation and availability are not supplied.\n  - Indexed file services, allocation, character encoding, collating sequence, and runtime initialization are deployment dependencies.\n  - Arithmetic has no ON SIZE ERROR handling. Intermediate and accumulated amounts can overflow even when individual inputs fit their pictures.\n  - Posting opens the indexed transaction file OUTPUT, not I-O. Preservation of pre-existing master records must not be assumed.\n  - REPROC references an unsupplied REPROCT control member. Supplied JCL describes intended infrastructure, not an executable guarantee.\n  - TRANREPT JCL has duplicate STEP05R names and an external SORT using a zoned-decimal card key, whereas COBOL card fields are alphanumeric.\npaths:\n  /transaction-posting-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Process an ordered daily transaction file\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBTRN02C with the request records as DALYTRAN. Empty input is\n        representable. XREFFILE is read-only; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are opened\n        I-O; TRANFILE and DALYREJS are opened OUTPUT.\n\n        For each record, card lookup INVALID KEY yields 0100. If that succeeds,\n        account lookup INVALID KEY yields 0101. Otherwise WS-TEMP-BAL\n        (S9(9)V99) is cycleCredit - cycleDebit + amount. Credit limit less\n        than that result yields 0102. Account expiration text less than the\n        first ten characters of originalTimestamp yields 0103, overwriting\n        0102 if both conditions hold. Equality passes both comparisons.\n        There are no active-status, positive-amount, card-format, type,\n        category, timestamp-syntax, or duplicate-ID business validations.\n\n        Rejected records are copied in full, including input processing\n        timestamp and filler, to the 350-byte portion of a 430-byte reject\n        record, followed by a four-digit reason and 76-character description.\n        Processing continues with the next record.\n\n        For accepted records, processingTimestamp is replaced by runtime\n        CURRENT-DATE formatted YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000. Other named fields\n        are copied. Output filler is not copied explicitly. First the category\n        balance keyed by resolved account, type, and category is created on\n        status 23 with initial balance equal to amount, or incremented.\n        Then current account balance is incremented; amount >= 0 is added\n        to cycle credit, otherwise the negative amount is added to cycle debit.\n        Finally the indexed transaction record is written under its ID.\n        These effects are sequential, not atomic.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109 and description\n        ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND, but the caller does not recheck it, write\n        a reject, or increment the reject count; transaction writing continues.\n        Duplicate transaction IDs are not screened and may fail at WRITE after\n        balance changes. Lookup routines for card and account do not perform\n        general file-status checks beyond their INVALID KEY clauses.\n\n        Normal completion displays counts of all input records and rejects.\n        RETURN-CODE is explicitly set to 4 only if reject count is positive.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Runtime bindings must supply XREFFILE, ACCTFILE, TCATBALF, TRANFILE, and DALYREJS with the organizations and access modes above.\n        - Missing card or account records remain admissible inputs and follow business rejection branches, rather than transport prevalidation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Run completed, possibly with rejects and RETURN-CODE 4.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactions, rejects]\n                properties:\n                  processedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  rejectedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime return code; only value 4 for a nonzero reject count is explicitly assigned by the source.\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Records successfully written to TRANFILE; indexed storage does not guarantee input-order retrieval.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  rejects:\n                    type: array\n                    description: DALYREJS records in input order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RejectedTransaction'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-generation-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest records from category balances\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBACT04C. TCATBALF is read sequentially in indexed key order\n        (account, type, category). ACCTFILE is opened I-O; XREFFILE and DISCGRP\n        are input; TRANSACT is sequential OUTPUT. This operation does not\n        insert generated records into the indexed transaction master and does\n        not post them through CBTRN02C.\n\n        On each account change, the previous account is rewritten by adding\n        accumulated interest to current balance and zeroing cycle credit and\n        cycle debit. The new account and its card cross-reference are read,\n        the latter by alternate account key. For every category balance the\n        disclosure key is account group, original category type, and original\n        category. A missing disclosure record (status 23) retries the lookup\n        with the group field set to DEFAULT padded to ten characters, keeping\n        type and category unchanged. Failure of that default lookup is fatal.\n\n        For each nonzero rate, monthly interest = categoryBalance * rate / 1200\n        assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED, truncating fractional cents when\n        representable. That amount is accumulated and one transaction is\n        emitted, even when the resulting amount is zero or negative. Zero rate\n        emits no transaction. Fees are an empty, unimplemented paragraph.\n\n        Generated ID is the full ten-character parameter plus a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001 for each run. Generated type is 01,\n        category is numeric 0005, source is System, description starts with\n        \"Int. for a/c \" followed by the eleven-digit account ID. Merchant ID is\n        zero, merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces, card is the alternate-key\n        cross-reference card. Original and processing timestamps are the same\n        runtime timestamp, not the parameter date. No ID uniqueness check exists.\n\n        The loop exits as soon as the read sets EOF. The apparent ELSE\n        performing final account update is not reached on normal EOF.\n        Consequently the last account group is not rewritten, although its\n        transactions have been generated. With one account group, no account\n        is rewritten; with empty category input, none is generated or rewritten.\n        TCATBALF is never updated by this program.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Account, disclosure, category-balance and cross-reference indexed files must be bound and accessible.\n        - Account alternate-key reads on XREFFILE must be supported; INTCALC supplies XREFFIL1 but the COBOL SELECT names XREFFILE.\n        - Missing accounts, alternate-key cross-references, and default disclosures are representable dependency failures, not request validation constraints.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Alternate account-key uniqueness and runtime path binding are not established; no choice among multiple cards is defined here.\n        - The six-digit suffix can overflow; no guard or collision handling is supplied.\n        - Description tail and transaction filler are not explicitly initialized in the write paragraph.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactionIdPrefix]\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: PARM-DATE PIC X(10); arbitrary text, not a validated date. PARM-LENGTH is not read by the program and is transport-supplied.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Category scan and closes completed; does not imply the final account was updated.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Sequential TRANSACT output in category-key scan order for nonzero rates.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-report-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce fixed-width transaction detail report records\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBTRN03C over the supplied sequential TRANFILE and DATEPARM\n        records, using read-only indexed CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, and TRANCATG.\n        TRANREPT is opened OUTPUT; no account or transaction balances change.\n\n        Reads only the first DATEPARM record. Its first ten characters are\n        start date, character eleven is ignored, and characters twelve through\n        twenty-one are end date; the remaining characters are unused.\n        Empty DATEPARM sets EOF before the transaction loop and produces no\n        report records. No date syntax, separator, or start/end ordering\n        validation is performed.\n\n        Processing timestamp characters 1:10 are compared inclusively with the\n        two parameter texts. Out-of-range input executes NEXT SENTENCE to\n        after the loop's terminating period, so it ends processing rather than\n        merely skipping that record. Therefore external prefiltering affects\n        observable results and is not silently performed by this operation.\n\n        For an in-range record, a changed card triggers an account-total line\n        for the previous card group (except before the first detail), followed\n        by cross-reference lookup. Type and composite type/category\n        descriptions are looked up for every detail. INVALID KEY on any of\n        these three lookups displays a diagnostic, reports status 23, and\n        calls CEE3ABD; unknown keys are not replaced with generic descriptions.\n\n        Input order is retained. Account totals actually delimit contiguous\n        card groups, not account-ID groups. No internal sort is implemented.\n        On the first detail four header lines are written. Before each detail,\n        if lineCounter MOD 20 = 0, page total and separator are written and\n        four headers follow. Headers, separators, details and group totals all\n        increment the counter; there is no reset on a new page. The report\n        carries transaction ID, resolved account ID, type and 15-character\n        description, category and 29-character description, source and edited\n        amount. Type/category master descriptions are truncated for display.\n\n        After a normal transaction EOF, the code still tests the transaction\n        buffer date. If in range, it adds the retained TRAN-AMT again to page\n        and account totals, writes page total (adding it to grand total), a\n        separator, and grand total. It does not write a final account total.\n        If the date test fails, NEXT SENTENCE bypasses those totals. This\n        contract exposes actual fixed-width lines rather than corrected totals.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG, and the output report file must be bound and accessible.\n        - Contiguous card ordering is needed for meaningful group totals, but unsorted input remains representable.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - EOF buffer retention and initial contents affect empty-input and final-total behavior; a mathematically correct grand total is not guaranteed.\n        - JCL separately filters processing dates using hardcoded constants and sorts by card; it does not establish that DATEPARM contains the same range.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential 80-character DATEPARM records; zero records and extra ignored records are representable.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Report program completed; output can be empty or partial due to its date-control flow.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    type: array\n                    description: TRANREPT records including padding, headings, separators, details, and totals as actually written.\n                    items:\n                      type: string\n                      minLength: 133\n                      maxLength: 133\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    TransportRejection:\n      description: Chosen HTTP rejection for JSON or picture representation errors; not a COBOL business rejection. No legacy error payload is defined.\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP mapping for a fatal program or dependency failure.\n        Checked non-00 opens, closes, output writes, and non-EOF sequential\n        reads display an error and file status and invoke CEE3ABD(999, 0).\n        Interest also treats unsuccessful account and cross-reference reads,\n        non-00/non-23 disclosure reads, failed default reads and account\n        rewrites as fatal. Posting permits category read 23 for creation but\n        aborts on other non-00 category reads and failed category writes or\n        rewrites. Reporting INVALID KEY lookups are fatal. These checks are\n        not generalized to routines that omit status handling.\n        Prior writes and output-file initialization may already have occurred;\n        there is no rollback or complete-result guarantee.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            type: object\n            description: Transport envelope for available observations; fields are optional because runtime failure may prevent their capture.\n            properties:\n              program:\n                type: string\n                enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n              diagnostics:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  type: string\n              fileStatus:\n                type: string\n                minLength: 2\n                maxLength: 2\n                description: Raw two-character status if observed. Posting reject-file close mistakenly displays XREFFILE status instead.\n              requestedAbendCode:\n                type: integer\n                const: 999\n  schemas:\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: PIC 9(9); no overflow guard.\n    Amount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -999999999.99\n      maximum: 999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(9)V99; negative and zero amounts remain admissible.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -9999999999.99\n      maximum: 9999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n      description: Eleven display digits, preserving leading zeros.\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2); no code enumeration is imposed.\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 9999\n      description: PIC 9(4), rendered as four digits in native records.\n    TimestampText:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: PIC X(26), not an ISO date-time validation. Generated values use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 without timezone.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required:\n        - transactionId\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n        - filler\n      description: CVTRA05Y and CVTRA06Y share this 350-character logical layout. Input filler is preserved on rejection, not explicitly copied on posting.\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16); nonnumeric and missing lookup keys are representable.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TimestampText'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TimestampText'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n    RejectedTransaction:\n      type: object\n      required: [transaction, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        transaction:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n          description: 0109 is assigned after account REWRITE failure but is not routed to the reject file.\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 76\n          description: |\n            Space-padded to 76 characters in the native trailer:\n            0100 INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND;\n            0101 ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND;\n            0102 OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION;\n            0103 TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION.\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: Persistent ACCTFILE record layout, not an account-management API or request-supplied replacement.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CardCrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 50-character indexed dependency; primary key is card number.\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: Persistent 50-character TCATBALF record keyed by accountId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroup:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 50-character DISCGRP record keyed by groupId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: number\n          minimum: -9999.99\n          maximum: 9999.99\n          multipleOf: 0.01\n          description: PIC S9(4)V99; zero suppresses generation, negative rates are not rejected.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 60-character TRANTYPE record keyed by typeCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 60-character TRANCATG record keyed by typeCode and categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\nx-persistent-dependencies:\n  posting:\n    input: [XREFFILE]\n    inputOutput: [ACCTFILE, TCATBALF]\n    output: [TRANFILE, DALYREJS]\n  interest:\n    input: [TCATBALF, XREFFILE, DISCGRP]\n    inputOutput: [ACCTFILE]\n    output: [TRANSACT]\n  reporting:\n    input: [CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG]\n    output: [TRANREPT]\nx-job-boundary:\n  description: |\n    POSTTRAN binds daily records and master files to CBTRN02C.\n    INTCALC binds CBACT04C output to SYSTRAN, not the transaction master.\n    COMBTRAN describes sorting a backup plus SYSTRAN by transaction ID and\n    IDCAMS REPRO into the master. TRANBKP describes backup, deletion and\n    redefinition of the transaction cluster. TRANREPT describes unload,\n    date filtering, sorting, and report generation. None of those utility\n    effects or ordering relationships is implicitly executed by these POSTs.\n    Generated interest records are not guaranteed to be visible to reporting\n    until explicitly supplied as report input or moved by external infrastructure."}

event: response.content_part.done
data: {"type":"response.content_part.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0c1bbaee4dd80661016aa3e80c461487d2ae45d60cc594c4d6","output_index":1,"part":{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for CBTRN02C posting, CBACT04C interest generation, and CBTRN03C\n    reporting. Each POST represents one program invocation, not an entire job\n    schedule. JSON arrays carry sequential input and output records in order;\n    indexed files remain deployment-bound persistent dependencies. HTTP paths,\n    JSON names, and status codes are chosen transport conventions, not COBOL\n    interfaces. A completed posting run may contain business rejects and still\n    returns HTTP 200. HTTP 500 represents an observed fatal execution path,\n    not a business validation rejection.\n\n    Fixed-width alphanumeric fields accept arbitrary text up to their picture\n    length, including blanks and unknown codes. Transport mapping right-pads\n    shorter text with spaces; it does not parse dates or validate card numbers.\n    Numeric JSON values represent valid numeric picture contents. No promise is\n    made about malformed native numeric encodings, arithmetic overflow, or\n    runtime availability. Output text may retain trailing spaces.\n\n    No operation implies transaction atomicity, rollback, retries, or execution\n    of SORT, IDCAMS, REPROC, backup, reload, or any subsequent batch program.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - CEE3ABD is called with code 999 and timing 0 but its implementation and availability are not supplied.\n  - Indexed file services, allocation, character encoding, collating sequence, and runtime initialization are deployment dependencies.\n  - Arithmetic has no ON SIZE ERROR handling. Intermediate and accumulated amounts can overflow even when individual inputs fit their pictures.\n  - Posting opens the indexed transaction file OUTPUT, not I-O. Preservation of pre-existing master records must not be assumed.\n  - REPROC references an unsupplied REPROCT control member. Supplied JCL describes intended infrastructure, not an executable guarantee.\n  - TRANREPT JCL has duplicate STEP05R names and an external SORT using a zoned-decimal card key, whereas COBOL card fields are alphanumeric.\npaths:\n  /transaction-posting-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Process an ordered daily transaction file\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBTRN02C with the request records as DALYTRAN. Empty input is\n        representable. XREFFILE is read-only; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are opened\n        I-O; TRANFILE and DALYREJS are opened OUTPUT.\n\n        For each record, card lookup INVALID KEY yields 0100. If that succeeds,\n        account lookup INVALID KEY yields 0101. Otherwise WS-TEMP-BAL\n        (S9(9)V99) is cycleCredit - cycleDebit + amount. Credit limit less\n        than that result yields 0102. Account expiration text less than the\n        first ten characters of originalTimestamp yields 0103, overwriting\n        0102 if both conditions hold. Equality passes both comparisons.\n        There are no active-status, positive-amount, card-format, type,\n        category, timestamp-syntax, or duplicate-ID business validations.\n\n        Rejected records are copied in full, including input processing\n        timestamp and filler, to the 350-byte portion of a 430-byte reject\n        record, followed by a four-digit reason and 76-character description.\n        Processing continues with the next record.\n\n        For accepted records, processingTimestamp is replaced by runtime\n        CURRENT-DATE formatted YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000. Other named fields\n        are copied. Output filler is not copied explicitly. First the category\n        balance keyed by resolved account, type, and category is created on\n        status 23 with initial balance equal to amount, or incremented.\n        Then current account balance is incremented; amount >= 0 is added\n        to cycle credit, otherwise the negative amount is added to cycle debit.\n        Finally the indexed transaction record is written under its ID.\n        These effects are sequential, not atomic.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109 and description\n        ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND, but the caller does not recheck it, write\n        a reject, or increment the reject count; transaction writing continues.\n        Duplicate transaction IDs are not screened and may fail at WRITE after\n        balance changes. Lookup routines for card and account do not perform\n        general file-status checks beyond their INVALID KEY clauses.\n\n        Normal completion displays counts of all input records and rejects.\n        RETURN-CODE is explicitly set to 4 only if reject count is positive.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Runtime bindings must supply XREFFILE, ACCTFILE, TCATBALF, TRANFILE, and DALYREJS with the organizations and access modes above.\n        - Missing card or account records remain admissible inputs and follow business rejection branches, rather than transport prevalidation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Run completed, possibly with rejects and RETURN-CODE 4.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactions, rejects]\n                properties:\n                  processedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  rejectedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime return code; only value 4 for a nonzero reject count is explicitly assigned by the source.\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Records successfully written to TRANFILE; indexed storage does not guarantee input-order retrieval.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  rejects:\n                    type: array\n                    description: DALYREJS records in input order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RejectedTransaction'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-generation-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest records from category balances\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBACT04C. TCATBALF is read sequentially in indexed key order\n        (account, type, category). ACCTFILE is opened I-O; XREFFILE and DISCGRP\n        are input; TRANSACT is sequential OUTPUT. This operation does not\n        insert generated records into the indexed transaction master and does\n        not post them through CBTRN02C.\n\n        On each account change, the previous account is rewritten by adding\n        accumulated interest to current balance and zeroing cycle credit and\n        cycle debit. The new account and its card cross-reference are read,\n        the latter by alternate account key. For every category balance the\n        disclosure key is account group, original category type, and original\n        category. A missing disclosure record (status 23) retries the lookup\n        with the group field set to DEFAULT padded to ten characters, keeping\n        type and category unchanged. Failure of that default lookup is fatal.\n\n        For each nonzero rate, monthly interest = categoryBalance * rate / 1200\n        assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED, truncating fractional cents when\n        representable. That amount is accumulated and one transaction is\n        emitted, even when the resulting amount is zero or negative. Zero rate\n        emits no transaction. Fees are an empty, unimplemented paragraph.\n\n        Generated ID is the full ten-character parameter plus a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001 for each run. Generated type is 01,\n        category is numeric 0005, source is System, description starts with\n        \"Int. for a/c \" followed by the eleven-digit account ID. Merchant ID is\n        zero, merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces, card is the alternate-key\n        cross-reference card. Original and processing timestamps are the same\n        runtime timestamp, not the parameter date. No ID uniqueness check exists.\n\n        The loop exits as soon as the read sets EOF. The apparent ELSE\n        performing final account update is not reached on normal EOF.\n        Consequently the last account group is not rewritten, although its\n        transactions have been generated. With one account group, no account\n        is rewritten; with empty category input, none is generated or rewritten.\n        TCATBALF is never updated by this program.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Account, disclosure, category-balance and cross-reference indexed files must be bound and accessible.\n        - Account alternate-key reads on XREFFILE must be supported; INTCALC supplies XREFFIL1 but the COBOL SELECT names XREFFILE.\n        - Missing accounts, alternate-key cross-references, and default disclosures are representable dependency failures, not request validation constraints.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Alternate account-key uniqueness and runtime path binding are not established; no choice among multiple cards is defined here.\n        - The six-digit suffix can overflow; no guard or collision handling is supplied.\n        - Description tail and transaction filler are not explicitly initialized in the write paragraph.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactionIdPrefix]\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: PARM-DATE PIC X(10); arbitrary text, not a validated date. PARM-LENGTH is not read by the program and is transport-supplied.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Category scan and closes completed; does not imply the final account was updated.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Sequential TRANSACT output in category-key scan order for nonzero rates.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-report-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce fixed-width transaction detail report records\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBTRN03C over the supplied sequential TRANFILE and DATEPARM\n        records, using read-only indexed CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, and TRANCATG.\n        TRANREPT is opened OUTPUT; no account or transaction balances change.\n\n        Reads only the first DATEPARM record. Its first ten characters are\n        start date, character eleven is ignored, and characters twelve through\n        twenty-one are end date; the remaining characters are unused.\n        Empty DATEPARM sets EOF before the transaction loop and produces no\n        report records. No date syntax, separator, or start/end ordering\n        validation is performed.\n\n        Processing timestamp characters 1:10 are compared inclusively with the\n        two parameter texts. Out-of-range input executes NEXT SENTENCE to\n        after the loop's terminating period, so it ends processing rather than\n        merely skipping that record. Therefore external prefiltering affects\n        observable results and is not silently performed by this operation.\n\n        For an in-range record, a changed card triggers an account-total line\n        for the previous card group (except before the first detail), followed\n        by cross-reference lookup. Type and composite type/category\n        descriptions are looked up for every detail. INVALID KEY on any of\n        these three lookups displays a diagnostic, reports status 23, and\n        calls CEE3ABD; unknown keys are not replaced with generic descriptions.\n\n        Input order is retained. Account totals actually delimit contiguous\n        card groups, not account-ID groups. No internal sort is implemented.\n        On the first detail four header lines are written. Before each detail,\n        if lineCounter MOD 20 = 0, page total and separator are written and\n        four headers follow. Headers, separators, details and group totals all\n        increment the counter; there is no reset on a new page. The report\n        carries transaction ID, resolved account ID, type and 15-character\n        description, category and 29-character description, source and edited\n        amount. Type/category master descriptions are truncated for display.\n\n        After a normal transaction EOF, the code still tests the transaction\n        buffer date. If in range, it adds the retained TRAN-AMT again to page\n        and account totals, writes page total (adding it to grand total), a\n        separator, and grand total. It does not write a final account total.\n        If the date test fails, NEXT SENTENCE bypasses those totals. This\n        contract exposes actual fixed-width lines rather than corrected totals.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG, and the output report file must be bound and accessible.\n        - Contiguous card ordering is needed for meaningful group totals, but unsorted input remains representable.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - EOF buffer retention and initial contents affect empty-input and final-total behavior; a mathematically correct grand total is not guaranteed.\n        - JCL separately filters processing dates using hardcoded constants and sorts by card; it does not establish that DATEPARM contains the same range.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential 80-character DATEPARM records; zero records and extra ignored records are representable.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Report program completed; output can be empty or partial due to its date-control flow.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    type: array\n                    description: TRANREPT records including padding, headings, separators, details, and totals as actually written.\n                    items:\n                      type: string\n                      minLength: 133\n                      maxLength: 133\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    TransportRejection:\n      description: Chosen HTTP rejection for JSON or picture representation errors; not a COBOL business rejection. No legacy error payload is defined.\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP mapping for a fatal program or dependency failure.\n        Checked non-00 opens, closes, output writes, and non-EOF sequential\n        reads display an error and file status and invoke CEE3ABD(999, 0).\n        Interest also treats unsuccessful account and cross-reference reads,\n        non-00/non-23 disclosure reads, failed default reads and account\n        rewrites as fatal. Posting permits category read 23 for creation but\n        aborts on other non-00 category reads and failed category writes or\n        rewrites. Reporting INVALID KEY lookups are fatal. These checks are\n        not generalized to routines that omit status handling.\n        Prior writes and output-file initialization may already have occurred;\n        there is no rollback or complete-result guarantee.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            type: object\n            description: Transport envelope for available observations; fields are optional because runtime failure may prevent their capture.\n            properties:\n              program:\n                type: string\n                enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n              diagnostics:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  type: string\n              fileStatus:\n                type: string\n                minLength: 2\n                maxLength: 2\n                description: Raw two-character status if observed. Posting reject-file close mistakenly displays XREFFILE status instead.\n              requestedAbendCode:\n                type: integer\n                const: 999\n  schemas:\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: PIC 9(9); no overflow guard.\n    Amount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -999999999.99\n      maximum: 999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(9)V99; negative and zero amounts remain admissible.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -9999999999.99\n      maximum: 9999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n      description: Eleven display digits, preserving leading zeros.\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2); no code enumeration is imposed.\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 9999\n      description: PIC 9(4), rendered as four digits in native records.\n    TimestampText:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: PIC X(26), not an ISO date-time validation. Generated values use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 without timezone.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required:\n        - transactionId\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n        - filler\n      description: CVTRA05Y and CVTRA06Y share this 350-character logical layout. Input filler is preserved on rejection, not explicitly copied on posting.\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16); nonnumeric and missing lookup keys are representable.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TimestampText'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TimestampText'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n    RejectedTransaction:\n      type: object\n      required: [transaction, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        transaction:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n          description: 0109 is assigned after account REWRITE failure but is not routed to the reject file.\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 76\n          description: |\n            Space-padded to 76 characters in the native trailer:\n            0100 INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND;\n            0101 ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND;\n            0102 OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION;\n            0103 TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION.\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: Persistent ACCTFILE record layout, not an account-management API or request-supplied replacement.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CardCrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 50-character indexed dependency; primary key is card number.\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: Persistent 50-character TCATBALF record keyed by accountId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroup:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 50-character DISCGRP record keyed by groupId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: number\n          minimum: -9999.99\n          maximum: 9999.99\n          multipleOf: 0.01\n          description: PIC S9(4)V99; zero suppresses generation, negative rates are not rejected.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 60-character TRANTYPE record keyed by typeCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 60-character TRANCATG record keyed by typeCode and categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\nx-persistent-dependencies:\n  posting:\n    input: [XREFFILE]\n    inputOutput: [ACCTFILE, TCATBALF]\n    output: [TRANFILE, DALYREJS]\n  interest:\n    input: [TCATBALF, XREFFILE, DISCGRP]\n    inputOutput: [ACCTFILE]\n    output: [TRANSACT]\n  reporting:\n    input: [CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG]\n    output: [TRANREPT]\nx-job-boundary:\n  description: |\n    POSTTRAN binds daily records and master files to CBTRN02C.\n    INTCALC binds CBACT04C output to SYSTRAN, not the transaction master.\n    COMBTRAN describes sorting a backup plus SYSTRAN by transaction ID and\n    IDCAMS REPRO into the master. TRANBKP describes backup, deletion and\n    redefinition of the transaction cluster. TRANREPT describes unload,\n    date filtering, sorting, and report generation. None of those utility\n    effects or ordering relationships is implicitly executed by these POSTs.\n    Generated interest records are not guaranteed to be visible to reporting\n    until explicitly supplied as report input or moved by external infrastructure."},"sequence_number":5374}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"id":"msg_0c1bbaee4dd80661016aa3e80c461487d2ae45d60cc594c4d6","type":"message","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for CBTRN02C posting, CBACT04C interest generation, and CBTRN03C\n    reporting. Each POST represents one program invocation, not an entire job\n    schedule. JSON arrays carry sequential input and output records in order;\n    indexed files remain deployment-bound persistent dependencies. HTTP paths,\n    JSON names, and status codes are chosen transport conventions, not COBOL\n    interfaces. A completed posting run may contain business rejects and still\n    returns HTTP 200. HTTP 500 represents an observed fatal execution path,\n    not a business validation rejection.\n\n    Fixed-width alphanumeric fields accept arbitrary text up to their picture\n    length, including blanks and unknown codes. Transport mapping right-pads\n    shorter text with spaces; it does not parse dates or validate card numbers.\n    Numeric JSON values represent valid numeric picture contents. No promise is\n    made about malformed native numeric encodings, arithmetic overflow, or\n    runtime availability. Output text may retain trailing spaces.\n\n    No operation implies transaction atomicity, rollback, retries, or execution\n    of SORT, IDCAMS, REPROC, backup, reload, or any subsequent batch program.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - CEE3ABD is called with code 999 and timing 0 but its implementation and availability are not supplied.\n  - Indexed file services, allocation, character encoding, collating sequence, and runtime initialization are deployment dependencies.\n  - Arithmetic has no ON SIZE ERROR handling. Intermediate and accumulated amounts can overflow even when individual inputs fit their pictures.\n  - Posting opens the indexed transaction file OUTPUT, not I-O. Preservation of pre-existing master records must not be assumed.\n  - REPROC references an unsupplied REPROCT control member. Supplied JCL describes intended infrastructure, not an executable guarantee.\n  - TRANREPT JCL has duplicate STEP05R names and an external SORT using a zoned-decimal card key, whereas COBOL card fields are alphanumeric.\npaths:\n  /transaction-posting-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Process an ordered daily transaction file\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBTRN02C with the request records as DALYTRAN. Empty input is\n        representable. XREFFILE is read-only; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are opened\n        I-O; TRANFILE and DALYREJS are opened OUTPUT.\n\n        For each record, card lookup INVALID KEY yields 0100. If that succeeds,\n        account lookup INVALID KEY yields 0101. Otherwise WS-TEMP-BAL\n        (S9(9)V99) is cycleCredit - cycleDebit + amount. Credit limit less\n        than that result yields 0102. Account expiration text less than the\n        first ten characters of originalTimestamp yields 0103, overwriting\n        0102 if both conditions hold. Equality passes both comparisons.\n        There are no active-status, positive-amount, card-format, type,\n        category, timestamp-syntax, or duplicate-ID business validations.\n\n        Rejected records are copied in full, including input processing\n        timestamp and filler, to the 350-byte portion of a 430-byte reject\n        record, followed by a four-digit reason and 76-character description.\n        Processing continues with the next record.\n\n        For accepted records, processingTimestamp is replaced by runtime\n        CURRENT-DATE formatted YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000. Other named fields\n        are copied. Output filler is not copied explicitly. First the category\n        balance keyed by resolved account, type, and category is created on\n        status 23 with initial balance equal to amount, or incremented.\n        Then current account balance is incremented; amount >= 0 is added\n        to cycle credit, otherwise the negative amount is added to cycle debit.\n        Finally the indexed transaction record is written under its ID.\n        These effects are sequential, not atomic.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109 and description\n        ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND, but the caller does not recheck it, write\n        a reject, or increment the reject count; transaction writing continues.\n        Duplicate transaction IDs are not screened and may fail at WRITE after\n        balance changes. Lookup routines for card and account do not perform\n        general file-status checks beyond their INVALID KEY clauses.\n\n        Normal completion displays counts of all input records and rejects.\n        RETURN-CODE is explicitly set to 4 only if reject count is positive.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Runtime bindings must supply XREFFILE, ACCTFILE, TCATBALF, TRANFILE, and DALYREJS with the organizations and access modes above.\n        - Missing card or account records remain admissible inputs and follow business rejection branches, rather than transport prevalidation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Run completed, possibly with rejects and RETURN-CODE 4.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [processedCount, rejectedCount, transactions, rejects]\n                properties:\n                  processedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  rejectedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Observed runtime return code; only value 4 for a nonzero reject count is explicitly assigned by the source.\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Records successfully written to TRANFILE; indexed storage does not guarantee input-order retrieval.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  rejects:\n                    type: array\n                    description: DALYREJS records in input order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RejectedTransaction'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-generation-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest records from category balances\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBACT04C. TCATBALF is read sequentially in indexed key order\n        (account, type, category). ACCTFILE is opened I-O; XREFFILE and DISCGRP\n        are input; TRANSACT is sequential OUTPUT. This operation does not\n        insert generated records into the indexed transaction master and does\n        not post them through CBTRN02C.\n\n        On each account change, the previous account is rewritten by adding\n        accumulated interest to current balance and zeroing cycle credit and\n        cycle debit. The new account and its card cross-reference are read,\n        the latter by alternate account key. For every category balance the\n        disclosure key is account group, original category type, and original\n        category. A missing disclosure record (status 23) retries the lookup\n        with the group field set to DEFAULT padded to ten characters, keeping\n        type and category unchanged. Failure of that default lookup is fatal.\n\n        For each nonzero rate, monthly interest = categoryBalance * rate / 1200\n        assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED, truncating fractional cents when\n        representable. That amount is accumulated and one transaction is\n        emitted, even when the resulting amount is zero or negative. Zero rate\n        emits no transaction. Fees are an empty, unimplemented paragraph.\n\n        Generated ID is the full ten-character parameter plus a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001 for each run. Generated type is 01,\n        category is numeric 0005, source is System, description starts with\n        \"Int. for a/c \" followed by the eleven-digit account ID. Merchant ID is\n        zero, merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces, card is the alternate-key\n        cross-reference card. Original and processing timestamps are the same\n        runtime timestamp, not the parameter date. No ID uniqueness check exists.\n\n        The loop exits as soon as the read sets EOF. The apparent ELSE\n        performing final account update is not reached on normal EOF.\n        Consequently the last account group is not rewritten, although its\n        transactions have been generated. With one account group, no account\n        is rewritten; with empty category input, none is generated or rewritten.\n        TCATBALF is never updated by this program.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Account, disclosure, category-balance and cross-reference indexed files must be bound and accessible.\n        - Account alternate-key reads on XREFFILE must be supported; INTCALC supplies XREFFIL1 but the COBOL SELECT names XREFFILE.\n        - Missing accounts, alternate-key cross-references, and default disclosures are representable dependency failures, not request validation constraints.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - Alternate account-key uniqueness and runtime path binding are not established; no choice among multiple cards is defined here.\n        - The six-digit suffix can overflow; no guard or collision handling is supplied.\n        - Description tail and transaction filler are not explicitly initialized in the write paragraph.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactionIdPrefix]\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: PARM-DATE PIC X(10); arbitrary text, not a validated date. PARM-LENGTH is not read by the program and is transport-supplied.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Category scan and closes completed; does not imply the final account was updated.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Sequential TRANSACT output in category-key scan order for nonzero rates.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-report-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce fixed-width transaction detail report records\n      description: |\n        Invokes CBTRN03C over the supplied sequential TRANFILE and DATEPARM\n        records, using read-only indexed CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, and TRANCATG.\n        TRANREPT is opened OUTPUT; no account or transaction balances change.\n\n        Reads only the first DATEPARM record. Its first ten characters are\n        start date, character eleven is ignored, and characters twelve through\n        twenty-one are end date; the remaining characters are unused.\n        Empty DATEPARM sets EOF before the transaction loop and produces no\n        report records. No date syntax, separator, or start/end ordering\n        validation is performed.\n\n        Processing timestamp characters 1:10 are compared inclusively with the\n        two parameter texts. Out-of-range input executes NEXT SENTENCE to\n        after the loop's terminating period, so it ends processing rather than\n        merely skipping that record. Therefore external prefiltering affects\n        observable results and is not silently performed by this operation.\n\n        For an in-range record, a changed card triggers an account-total line\n        for the previous card group (except before the first detail), followed\n        by cross-reference lookup. Type and composite type/category\n        descriptions are looked up for every detail. INVALID KEY on any of\n        these three lookups displays a diagnostic, reports status 23, and\n        calls CEE3ABD; unknown keys are not replaced with generic descriptions.\n\n        Input order is retained. Account totals actually delimit contiguous\n        card groups, not account-ID groups. No internal sort is implemented.\n        On the first detail four header lines are written. Before each detail,\n        if lineCounter MOD 20 = 0, page total and separator are written and\n        four headers follow. Headers, separators, details and group totals all\n        increment the counter; there is no reset on a new page. The report\n        carries transaction ID, resolved account ID, type and 15-character\n        description, category and 29-character description, source and edited\n        amount. Type/category master descriptions are truncated for display.\n\n        After a normal transaction EOF, the code still tests the transaction\n        buffer date. If in range, it adds the retained TRAN-AMT again to page\n        and account totals, writes page total (adding it to grand total), a\n        separator, and grand total. It does not write a final account total.\n        If the date test fails, NEXT SENTENCE bypasses those totals. This\n        contract exposes actual fixed-width lines rather than corrected totals.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG, and the output report file must be bound and accessible.\n        - Contiguous card ordering is needed for meaningful group totals, but unsorted input remains representable.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - EOF buffer retention and initial contents affect empty-input and final-total behavior; a mathematically correct grand total is not guaranteed.\n        - JCL separately filters processing dates using hardcoded constants and sorts by card; it does not establish that DATEPARM contains the same range.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential 80-character DATEPARM records; zero records and extra ignored records are representable.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Report program completed; output can be empty or partial due to its date-control flow.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    type: array\n                    description: TRANREPT records including padding, headings, separators, details, and totals as actually written.\n                    items:\n                      type: string\n                      minLength: 133\n                      maxLength: 133\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportRejection'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    TransportRejection:\n      description: Chosen HTTP rejection for JSON or picture representation errors; not a COBOL business rejection. No legacy error payload is defined.\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP mapping for a fatal program or dependency failure.\n        Checked non-00 opens, closes, output writes, and non-EOF sequential\n        reads display an error and file status and invoke CEE3ABD(999, 0).\n        Interest also treats unsuccessful account and cross-reference reads,\n        non-00/non-23 disclosure reads, failed default reads and account\n        rewrites as fatal. Posting permits category read 23 for creation but\n        aborts on other non-00 category reads and failed category writes or\n        rewrites. Reporting INVALID KEY lookups are fatal. These checks are\n        not generalized to routines that omit status handling.\n        Prior writes and output-file initialization may already have occurred;\n        there is no rollback or complete-result guarantee.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            type: object\n            description: Transport envelope for available observations; fields are optional because runtime failure may prevent their capture.\n            properties:\n              program:\n                type: string\n                enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n              diagnostics:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  type: string\n              fileStatus:\n                type: string\n                minLength: 2\n                maxLength: 2\n                description: Raw two-character status if observed. Posting reject-file close mistakenly displays XREFFILE status instead.\n              requestedAbendCode:\n                type: integer\n                const: 999\n  schemas:\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: PIC 9(9); no overflow guard.\n    Amount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -999999999.99\n      maximum: 999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(9)V99; negative and zero amounts remain admissible.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -9999999999.99\n      maximum: 9999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n      description: Eleven display digits, preserving leading zeros.\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2); no code enumeration is imposed.\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 9999\n      description: PIC 9(4), rendered as four digits in native records.\n    TimestampText:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: PIC X(26), not an ISO date-time validation. Generated values use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 without timezone.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required:\n        - transactionId\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n        - filler\n      description: CVTRA05Y and CVTRA06Y share this 350-character logical layout. Input filler is preserved on rejection, not explicitly copied on posting.\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16); nonnumeric and missing lookup keys are representable.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TimestampText'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TimestampText'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n    RejectedTransaction:\n      type: object\n      required: [transaction, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        transaction:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n          description: 0109 is assigned after account REWRITE failure but is not routed to the reject file.\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 76\n          description: |\n            Space-padded to 76 characters in the native trailer:\n            0100 INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND;\n            0101 ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND;\n            0102 OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION;\n            0103 TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION.\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: Persistent ACCTFILE record layout, not an account-management API or request-supplied replacement.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CardCrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 50-character indexed dependency; primary key is card number.\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: Persistent 50-character TCATBALF record keyed by accountId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroup:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 50-character DISCGRP record keyed by groupId, typeCode, categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: number\n          minimum: -9999.99\n          maximum: 9999.99\n          multipleOf: 0.01\n          description: PIC S9(4)V99; zero suppresses generation, negative rates are not rejected.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 60-character TRANTYPE record keyed by typeCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: Read-only 60-character TRANCATG record keyed by typeCode and categoryCode.\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\nx-persistent-dependencies:\n  posting:\n    input: [XREFFILE]\n    inputOutput: [ACCTFILE, TCATBALF]\n    output: [TRANFILE, DALYREJS]\n  interest:\n    input: [TCATBALF, XREFFILE, DISCGRP]\n    inputOutput: [ACCTFILE]\n    output: [TRANSACT]\n  reporting:\n    input: [CARDXREF, TRANTYPE, TRANCATG]\n    output: [TRANREPT]\nx-job-boundary:\n  description: |\n    POSTTRAN binds daily records and master files to CBTRN02C.\n    INTCALC binds CBACT04C output to SYSTRAN, not the transaction master.\n    COMBTRAN describes sorting a backup plus SYSTRAN by transaction ID and\n    IDCAMS REPRO into the master. TRANBKP describes backup, deletion and\n    redefinition of the transaction cluster. TRANREPT describes unload,\n    date filtering, sorting, and report generation. None of those utility\n    effects or ordering relationships is implicitly executed by these POSTs.\n    Generated interest records are not guaranteed to be visible to reporting\n    until explicitly supplied as report input or moved by external infrastructure."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"},"output_index":1,"sequence_number":5375}

